            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain and anxiety are among the recurring complaints in patients with a subarachnoid haemorrhage. A team assessed the efficacy and quality of pain management in a clinical neuroradiology unit. A global pain management procedure, including antalgic drug protocols and recommendations, was then put in place.</AbstractText>
